A new handle comes from calloc(), and openconnect_vpninfo_new() sets cmd_fd to
-1 but leaves cmd_fd_write at zero. openconnect_vpninfo_free() closes both when
cmd_fd_write >= 0. So freeing a handle that never called
openconnect_setup_cmd_pipe() closes file descriptor 0: standard input the
first time, and after that whatever the process has since opened as 0.

Set it to -1 with the others, which is what the test in
openconnect_vpninfo_free() and the one in check_cmd_fd() expect.

--- a/library.c
+++ b/library.c
@@ -196,6 +196,7 @@
 	vpninfo->dtls_fd = -1;
 	vpninfo->need_poll_cmd_fd = -1;
 	vpninfo->cmd_fd = -1;
+	vpninfo->cmd_fd_write = -1;
 	init_pkt_queue(&vpninfo->free_queue);
 	init_pkt_queue(&vpninfo->incoming_queue);
 	init_pkt_queue(&vpninfo->outgoing_queue);
